      "message": "refactor(app): tool-number follow-ups of #2488\n\n- Split crates/app/src/commands/tool_import.rs (401 lines): ImportMode\n  and ImportReport move to commands/tool_import_report.rs (97 lines),\n  re-exported from tool_import, so no path changes. tool_import.rs is\n  now 312 lines.\n- Split crates/app/tests/tool_numbers.rs (476 lines): the numbers that\n  never shift (#2442) and the legacy loads move to\n  tests/tool_numbers/stable.rs. The #[test] count goes from 10 to 13.\n- Two legacy-load tests: a file whose entity order is not the name order\n  (the freeze numbers by name), and a file that mixes a carried number\n  with unnumbered tools.\n- tool_numbers::numbers no longer gives an unnumbered tool u32::MAX when\n  no number is free: the new tool_numbers::assign refuses it by name, and\n  numbers() returns a Result. The post and the import propagate the\n  refusal, clash() reports it, number_of / next_free read it as None.\n- SetToolNumber keeps its number as a u32 (new already refuses None) and\n  exposes number(), so the UI status has no dead \"number cleared\" arm.\n\nPinned by tool_numbers: an_unnumbered_tool_with_no_free_number_is_refused_by_name,\nstable::a_legacy_project_numbers_by_name_order_not_by_document_order,\nstable::a_legacy_project_mixing_numbered_and_unnumbered_tools_keeps_both.\n\nFixes #2517\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
